@startuml organization-autonomy-governance
title Organization / Autonomy / Governance Boundary ; per ADR-ES-021 section 12 + CR-ES-021 section 13

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Autonomous Organization" as AO

class "Objectives" as Obj
class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraints" as Con
class "Accountability" as Acct
class "Governance" as Gov
class "Escalation" as Esc
class "Observation" as Obs

AO --> Obj : pursues
AO --> Auth : operates-within
AO --> Pol : governed-by
AO --> Con : constrained-by
AO --> Acct : accountable-under
AO --> Gov : operates-under
AO --> Esc : escalates-to
AO --> Obs : observation-under

note bottom of AO
  Autonomy is bounded by 7 governance fences. Per ADR-ES-021
  section 12: autonomy does NOT imply unlimited authority, no
  governance, no accountability, no human oversight, or
  unrestricted decision rights.
end note

@enduml
